<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AnalysisLevel>preview</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>AllEnabledByDefault</AnalysisMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Promptuarium</PackageId>
    <Title>Promptuarium</Title>
    <Description>Promptuarium is a versatile, tree-based data structure to store or exchange data and metadata efficiently (in binary format). Written in pure C#, can be used in F#, too.</Description>
    <PackageTags>promptuarium binary tree serialization space-efficient limitless container</PackageTags>
    <ReleaseNotes>New: Promptuarium.Serializer, a separate, experimental package (opt-in PRMTSER000): .NET objects to trees and back, without JSON, in the layout of SERIALIZER_FORMAT.md (PRMT:GEN1-LE, PRMT:CFG1-LE or a signature of the application), with comments. pedit and PStudio show the metadata before the data. PStudio: only the forms that give a content back byte for byte are offered; the tags and the type codes of the serializer layout by name; the chosen forms are remembered for every file (View / Reset Types forgets them); File / Open Recent; the settings are kept. GetStatistics().ToString() lists the metadata lines first. The library API and the binary format are unchanged.</ReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>ppak and ppakz are tools now (tools/PPak, tools/PPakZ), installed with PStudio and pedit by the Windows installer, the Debian package and the RPM package (man ppak, man ppakz). ppakz: the signature is PRMT:PPAKZ1-LE, the flags and the kinds are ushorts from 0x100, so they never look like the tags of the serializer, and the compression algorithm is stored next to every content (0x100: gzip); as in ppak, only the names and the contents are mandatory, a discrepancy in the additional information is a warning (verify, unpack --strict), and the decompressed contents are limited by --max-size (4 GiB by default). Archives of the earlier ppakz format are not read. The library, its API and the binary format are unchanged since 8.1.0.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
